  "configuration_id": "config_038",
  "reason": "The current best is config_036 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, ViT-L, avgpool, concat) at 0.7150 acc. In RNA-only experiments, avgpool consistently outperformed transformer (0.5907 vs 0.5191 for PCA), but the multimodal setting introduces cross-modal interactions that could change this dynamic. Config_038 is the cleanest single-variable test against the best configuration—it changes only aggregation from avgpool to transformer while keeping scvi_n200, ViT-L, multiprofile, and concat fusion fixed. This isolates whether transformer aggregation can better model multi-profile interactions when combined with image features. If it improves, we find a new best; if not, we confirm avgpool is optimal and reduce uncertainty for the final experiment. With only 1 experiment remaining after this, testing the most direct extension of the current best is the highest-value use of the budget."
}

